<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bootstrap.processes="https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/processes/ns/"
 xmlns:cat-harness.processes="https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/processes/ns/" xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL"
                  xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI"
                  xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC"
                  xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI"
                  id="Definitions_ContentChangeReviewCommittee"
                  targetNamespace="https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/workflows"
                  exporter="folio-assistant" exporterVersion="0.1.0">
  <bpmn:import namespace="https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/processes/ns/" location="https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/processes/ns.jsonld" importType="http://www.w3.org/ns/json-ld"/>
  <bpmn:resource id="review-coordinator" name="Review coordinator"/>
  <bpmn:resource id="reviewer" name="Reviewer / SME"/>

  <bpmn:collaboration id="Collaboration_ContentChangeReviewCommittee">
    <bpmn:participant id="Participant_ContentChangeReviewCommittee" name="Committee review of a content change" processRef="Process_ContentChangeReviewCommittee" />
  </bpmn:collaboration>

  <bpmn:process id="Process_ContentChangeReviewCommittee" name="Committee review of a content change" isExecutable="false">
    <bpmn:documentation>The review committee's review of one staged content change, ending in an approval or a request for changes: compare staged against main, slice the change and review each slice, settle withdrawn comments and disputed findings, gate on coverage, review the editorial dependencies and the impact, and decide.

Called from content-change-review when the author submits. Which end it reaches is what the caller's GW_CommitteeApproved reads. Organising the review is the review coordinator's lane and deciding it is the committee's. Merging is not here: it is a separate, confirmed act in content-change-review-publish.</bpmn:documentation>
    <bpmn:laneSet id="LaneSet_ContentChangeReviewCommittee">
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_Reviewer" name="Review Committee" partitionElementRef="reviewer">
        <bpmn:documentation>Compares staged against main, reviews the slices it is assigned (review-task.bpmn, one call per slice), takes a disputed finding to adjudication, judges the impact assessment, and decides. Task_Approve records the approval; merging is a separate, confirmed act in the publish phase. A rejection ends this phase with changes requested, and the caller routes it to Task_Iterate in the agent's lane rather than to the author.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Start_Reviewer</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_CompareBeforeAfter</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Call_ReviewSlices</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>GW_Withdraw</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_WithdrawComment</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>GW_Disputed_Join</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>GW_Disputed</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Call_Adjudication</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_ReviewUses</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_ReviewImpact</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>GW_Approved</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_RequestChanges</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End_ChangesRequested</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Approve</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End_Reviewer</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_Coordinator" name="Review Coordinator" partitionElementRef="review-coordinator">
        <bpmn:documentation>Organises a review large enough to need organising, and decides nothing about the content: ingests the reviewers' tagged comments, slices the change into pieces a reviewer can hold, assigns each slice to a review lane, and watches coverage until every changed block has a verdict or a reasoned waiver. A separate role from the editor: organising a review and deciding its outcome are different accountabilities.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_IngestComments</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_SliceAndAssign</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>GW_Covered_Join</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>GW_Covered</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
    </bpmn:laneSet>

    <bpmn:startEvent id="Start_Reviewer" name="PR submitted for review">
      <bpmn:outgoing>r1</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:startEvent>
    <bpmn:task id="Task_CompareBeforeAfter" name="Compare main vs staging">
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="staging-review"/>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="visual-diff"/>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="rendered-impact"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>

      <bpmn:documentation>
        The review starts from the Change Set's RENDERED list (skill
        rendered-impact): every rendered file the change alters, predicted
        from each renderer's dependency cone and checked against the build.
        The reviewer opens every content page on it, not only the pages the
        author mentions; index files are listed but not reviewed. An input
        the renderer could not place is shown as not known, never as no
        change.
        Review committee opens both URLs side by side:
        - Main site: &lt;pages-url&gt;/ (current published state)
        - Staging: &lt;pages-url&gt;/branches/&lt;branch-slug&gt;/
        The staging banner shows the commit SHA so they can verify
        what they are reviewing matches the PR. A changed figure, diagram
        or table is also pictured before and after on the review page,
        with the share of changed pixels in words (skill visual-diff,
        Tool folio-block-screenshots). Anything the staging job cannot
        picture (page chrome, scroll behaviour, a PDF page, an IG page) is
        in the agent's before/after preview (skill before-after-preview).
      </bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>r1</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>r2</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:task id="Task_IngestComments" name="Ingest tagged review comments">
      <bpmn:documentation>Every PR conversation comment that starts with `block: &lt;label&gt;` becomes a `review-comment/1.0.0` todo (open), idempotently, and is published with the preview as `review-comments.json`. The staging workflow runs this on every push and on every tagged comment; the coordinator owns that it has run before slicing, because the slices are cut around what reviewers have already said. This is the `ingest` transition of REVIEW_TRANSITIONS. Uses `folio-review-comments`.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="review-comments" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>r2</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>c1</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:task id="Task_SliceAndAssign" name="Slice the change and assign reviewers">
      <bpmn:documentation>From the ChangeSet, its rendered list (skill rendered-impact: each changed rendered page is assigned like a changed block) and the heat map on the review page: cut the change into slices a reviewer can hold (usually a section, or a run of sections where the heat map clusters), and assign each slice to a review lane by what it contains — clinical content to a clinical SME, a decision table to a QC reviewer, prose to a narrative reviewer. A block that needs no review (a pure rename, say) is WAIVED here with a written reason, which is what the coverage gate counts. Re-entered from GW_Covered when coverage is incomplete: the uncovered blocks become new slices.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="review-heatmap" />
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="staging-review" />
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="rendered-impact" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>c1</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>c8</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>c2</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:callActivity id="Call_ReviewSlices" name="Review each slice" calledElement="Process_Review">
      <bpmn:documentation>review-task.bpmn, once per slice, in parallel lanes by role. What kind of thing changed decides which review the slice descends into; the reviewer takes on that inner lane's role for the call only. Each reviewer gives the slice's blocks a verdict, and comments on the pull request with the `block:` tag where something needs saying.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="content-review" />
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="review-comments" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>c2</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>c3</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:callActivity>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="GW_Withdraw" name="A comment withdrawn?">
      <bpmn:documentation>Asked after the slices are reviewed: did a reviewer withdraw a comment? `Yes` records the withdrawal first; either way the flow then asks whether a finding is disputed.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>c3</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>c4</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>c5</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:task id="Task_WithdrawComment" name="Withdraw a review comment">
      <bpmn:documentation>The reviewer who made a comment takes it back (it was a misreading, or a later slice answered it). Recorded with `folio-review-comment-move --to withdrawn`, committed to the edit-set's feature branch like every status change. This is the `withdraw` transition of REVIEW_TRANSITIONS.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="review-comments" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>c4</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>c6</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="GW_Disputed_Join">
      <bpmn:documentation>Brings the paths together before the decision after it, so that decision only splits.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>c5</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>c6</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_GW_Disputed_Join</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="GW_Disputed" name="A finding disputed?">
      <bpmn:documentation>Is any finding disputed between author and reviewer? `Yes` goes to adjudication; `No` goes on to check that every changed block was reviewed.</bpmn:documentation>
      
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_GW_Disputed_Join</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>c7</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>c9</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:callActivity id="Call_Adjudication" name="Adjudicate the disagreement" calledElement="Process_Adjudication">
      <bpmn:documentation>adjudication.bpmn. When the editor and a reviewer, or two reviewers, disagree about a finding, an adjudicator settles it and records why; the review comment moves to `adjudicated` with the Decision that closed it.

Permitted answers: `stands` — the finding is right and the author addresses it; `withdrawn` — the finding is wrong and the comment closes. Recorded on the comment, not branched: either way the flow goes on to the coverage check.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="adjudication" />
        <cat-harness.processes:adjudication codes="stands withdrawn" list="adjudication-content-finding"/>
        <cat-harness.processes:fulfilment kinds="person agent" reason="the restriction Process_Adjudication states on A_Adjudicate, restated here because this is where the enum is declared; the engine refuses system or external on any step carrying cat-harness.processes:adjudication."/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>c7</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>c10</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:callActivity>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="GW_Covered_Join">
      <bpmn:documentation>Brings the paths together before the decision after it, so that decision only splits.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>c9</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>c10</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_GW_Covered_Join</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="GW_Covered" name="Every changed block and page reviewed?">
      <bpmn:documentation>Computed, not chosen: `decisions/review-coverage-gate.dmn` reads `uncoveredBlocks` (changed blocks with neither a verdict nor a reasoned waiver) and `openDefects`, and, where the build published a rendered impact, `unreviewedPages`, `undeterminedInputs` and `missedPages` with their `rendered` and `measured` statuses (skill rendered-impact). Resolved comments are not coverage, and coverage is not approval — that is GW_Approved.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <cat-harness.processes:decision ref="decisions/review-coverage-gate.dmn#Decision_ReviewCoverageGate" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_GW_Covered_Join</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>c8</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>c11</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:task id="Task_ReviewUses" name="Review the editorial dependencies">
      <bpmn:documentation>
        `uses[]` is what a READER must have read to follow the block — never
        populated from the formal dependency graph. Once every changed block
        is covered, the committee checks the editorial dependencies of the
        change as a whole before judging its impact. Reading order is a
        property of folio content, so the step belongs to the content
        process, which reaches the harness's review by calling DOWN into
        `review-task`.
      </bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements><bootstrap.processes:skill ref="uses-editorial-review"/></bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>c11</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>c11b</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:task id="Task_ReviewImpact" name="Review impact assessment">
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="content-review"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>

      <bpmn:documentation>
        Committee reviews the agent's impact assessment:
        - Were all downstream effects identified?
        - Are the indicator changes acceptable?
        - Does the logic change match the narrative intent?
      </bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>c11b</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>r3</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="GW_Approved" name="Changes approved?">
      <bpmn:documentation>The committee's decision on the impact assessment. `No` requests changes; `Yes` approves.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>r3</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>r4</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>r6</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:task id="Task_RequestChanges" name="Request changes">
      <bpmn:documentation>
        Committee provides feedback. PR stays open.
        Author and agent iterate further.
      </bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="content-review" />
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="content-review" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>r4</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>r5</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_ChangesRequested" name="changes requested">
      <bpmn:incoming>r5</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:task id="Task_Approve" name="Approve">
      <bpmn:documentation>
        The committee approves the change: the judgement, recorded with the
        evidence it rests on. Approving is not merging: a self-authored
        change cannot be approved through GitHub's own review (the approver
        may not be the PR's author), and a merge needs the owner's explicit
        confirmation whoever approved.
      </bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="decision-audit" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>r6</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>r8</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_Reviewer" name="approved">
      <bpmn:incoming>r8</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>

    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="r1" sourceRef="Start_Reviewer" targetRef="Task_CompareBeforeAfter" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="r2" sourceRef="Task_CompareBeforeAfter" targetRef="Task_IngestComments" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="c1" sourceRef="Task_IngestComments" targetRef="Task_SliceAndAssign" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="c2" sourceRef="Task_SliceAndAssign" targetRef="Call_ReviewSlices" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="c3" sourceRef="Call_ReviewSlices" targetRef="GW_Withdraw" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="c4" name="Yes" sourceRef="GW_Withdraw" targetRef="Task_WithdrawComment" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="c5" name="No" sourceRef="GW_Withdraw" targetRef="GW_Disputed_Join" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="c6" sourceRef="Task_WithdrawComment" targetRef="GW_Disputed_Join" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_GW_Disputed_Join" sourceRef="GW_Disputed_Join" targetRef="GW_Disputed"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="c7" name="Yes" sourceRef="GW_Disputed" targetRef="Call_Adjudication" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="c9" name="No" sourceRef="GW_Disputed" targetRef="GW_Covered_Join" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="c10" sourceRef="Call_Adjudication" targetRef="GW_Covered_Join" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_GW_Covered_Join" sourceRef="GW_Covered_Join" targetRef="GW_Covered"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="c8" name="no" sourceRef="GW_Covered" targetRef="Task_SliceAndAssign" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="c11" name="yes" sourceRef="GW_Covered" targetRef="Task_ReviewUses" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="c11b" sourceRef="Task_ReviewUses" targetRef="Task_ReviewImpact" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="r3" sourceRef="Task_ReviewImpact" targetRef="GW_Approved" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="r4" name="No" sourceRef="GW_Approved" targetRef="Task_RequestChanges" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="r5" sourceRef="Task_RequestChanges" targetRef="End_ChangesRequested" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="r6" name="Yes" sourceRef="GW_Approved" targetRef="Task_Approve" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="r8" sourceRef="Task_Approve" targetRef="End_Reviewer" />
  </bpmn:process>

  <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="BPMNDiagram_ContentChangeReviewCommittee">
    <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="BPMNPlane_ContentChangeReviewCommittee" bpmnElement="Collaboration_ContentChangeReviewCommittee">
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Participant_ContentChangeReviewCommittee_di" bpmnElement="Participant_ContentChangeReviewCommittee" isHorizontal="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="100" y="80" width="1380" height="450" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Lane_Reviewer_di" bpmnElement="Lane_Reviewer" isHorizontal="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="130" y="80" width="1350" height="290" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Lane_Coordinator_di" bpmnElement="Lane_Coordinator" isHorizontal="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="130" y="370" width="1350" height="160" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Start_Reviewer_di" bpmnElement="Start_Reviewer">
        <dc:Bounds x="180" y="137" width="36" height="36" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="160" y="177" width="85" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_CompareBeforeAfter_di" bpmnElement="Task_CompareBeforeAfter">
        <dc:Bounds x="250" y="95" width="120" height="120" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_IngestComments_di" bpmnElement="Task_IngestComments">
        <dc:Bounds x="250" y="385" width="120" height="120" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_SliceAndAssign_di" bpmnElement="Task_SliceAndAssign">
        <dc:Bounds x="410" y="385" width="120" height="120" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Call_ReviewSlices_di" bpmnElement="Call_ReviewSlices">
        <dc:Bounds x="410" y="95" width="120" height="120" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="GW_Withdraw_di" bpmnElement="GW_Withdraw">
        <dc:Bounds x="585" y="130" width="50" height="50" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="565" y="90" width="90" height="35" /></bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_WithdrawComment_di" bpmnElement="Task_WithdrawComment">
        <dc:Bounds x="550" y="230" width="120" height="120" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_GW_Disputed_Join" bpmnElement="GW_Disputed_Join" isMarkerVisible="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="705" y="130" width="50" height="50" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="GW_Disputed_di" bpmnElement="GW_Disputed">
        <dc:Bounds x="795" y="130" width="50" height="50" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="775" y="90" width="90" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Call_Adjudication_di" bpmnElement="Call_Adjudication">
        <dc:Bounds x="760" y="230" width="120" height="120" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_GW_Covered_Join" bpmnElement="GW_Covered_Join" isMarkerVisible="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="915" y="420" width="50" height="50" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="GW_Covered_di" bpmnElement="GW_Covered">
        <dc:Bounds x="995" y="420" width="50" height="50" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="1055" y="425" width="180" height="40" /></bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_ReviewUses_di" bpmnElement="Task_ReviewUses">
        <dc:Bounds x="940" y="95" width="120" height="120" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_ReviewImpact_di" bpmnElement="Task_ReviewImpact">
        <dc:Bounds x="1090" y="95" width="120" height="120" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="GW_Approved_di" bpmnElement="GW_Approved">
        <dc:Bounds x="1245" y="130" width="50" height="50" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="1225" y="90" width="90" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_RequestChanges_di" bpmnElement="Task_RequestChanges">
        <dc:Bounds x="1210" y="230" width="120" height="120" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="End_ChangesRequested_di" bpmnElement="End_ChangesRequested">
        <dc:Bounds x="1390" y="272" width="36" height="36" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="1365" y="312" width="86" height="28" /></bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_Approve_di" bpmnElement="Task_Approve">
        <dc:Bounds x="1330" y="95" width="120" height="120" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="End_Reviewer_di" bpmnElement="End_Reviewer">
        <dc:Bounds x="1372" y="228" width="36" height="36" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="1415" y="236" width="60" height="20" /></bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="r1_di" bpmnElement="r1">
        <di:waypoint x="216" y="155" />
        <di:waypoint x="250" y="155" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="r2_di" bpmnElement="r2">
        <di:waypoint x="310" y="215" />
        <di:waypoint x="310" y="385" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="c1_di" bpmnElement="c1">
        <di:waypoint x="370" y="445" />
        <di:waypoint x="410" y="445" />
